1
00:00:33,908 --> 00:00:35,243
Are you in position?

2
00:00:36,036 --> 00:00:37,746
<i>All set.</i>

3
00:00:43,334 --> 00:00:44,836
Thank you.

4
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:54,179
Hey. The trunk.
What are you doing, slowpoke?

5
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:56,514
He’s here.

6
00:00:56,598 --> 00:00:59,976
That’s Ishikawa,
the president of River Productions.

7
00:01:02,103 --> 00:01:04,856
He’s got that same sleazy face as always.

8
00:01:04,939 --> 00:01:06,816
Alright, Habu, I’m counting on you.

9
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:08,860
-Here is your room key.
-Thanks.

10
00:01:08,943 --> 00:01:10,361
Enjoy your stay.

11
00:01:11,946 --> 00:01:14,365
-What are you doing? Leave already.
-I'm sorry.

12
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:16,409
Sir, I will guide you to your room.

13
00:01:16,493 --> 00:01:18,578
No, thank you. It's all right.

14
00:01:18,661 --> 00:01:20,497
-I'll carry your luggage.
-I'm fine.

15
00:01:21,206 --> 00:01:23,458
-Please, allow me--
-I told you…

16
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:25,668
I don't need help.

17
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:27,212
My apologies.

18
00:01:27,295 --> 00:01:28,630
Seriously!

19
00:01:30,965 --> 00:01:32,175
Leave it to me.

20
00:01:35,762 --> 00:01:38,056
Oh, excuse me.

21
00:01:38,139 --> 00:01:40,141
-Which floor?
-18th floor, please.

22
00:01:41,476 --> 00:01:43,186
Thank you.

23
00:01:49,526 --> 00:01:51,569
-The 19th floor.
-<i>Understood.</i>

24
00:01:51,653 --> 00:01:54,114
<i>The 19th floor, right? Heading there now.</i>

25
00:02:02,413 --> 00:02:03,915
Room 1926.

26
00:02:27,897 --> 00:02:30,358
His room key is in
the left back pocket of his pants.

27
00:02:37,365 --> 00:02:39,325
-Ow! Hey!
-Ouch!

28
00:02:39,409 --> 00:02:41,953
Oh no, my racing tickets!

29
00:02:42,036 --> 00:02:43,830
Watch it, idiot.

30
00:02:44,706 --> 00:02:46,457
Huh? My winning ticket is gone.

31
00:02:46,541 --> 00:02:50,169
-Hey! Did you take it?
-I didn't. What the heck?

32
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:52,922
-That's my phone.
-Your back pockets.

33
00:02:53,006 --> 00:02:54,424
Hey, that's creepy, man.

34
00:02:55,008 --> 00:02:57,510
-Huh?
-Don't take my wallet!

35
00:02:57,594 --> 00:03:00,138
-I don't know about your ticket!
-Oh, sorry!

36
00:03:00,221 --> 00:03:01,431
I found it.

37
00:03:02,265 --> 00:03:03,600
Sorry.

38
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:21,326
Is this really okay?

39
00:03:21,409 --> 00:03:23,536
It's fine.

40
00:03:25,788 --> 00:03:27,665
It's locked!

41
00:03:28,207 --> 00:03:29,709
Four, one, zero.

42
00:03:29,792 --> 00:03:31,377
Two, two, three.

43
00:03:31,461 --> 00:03:33,254
That's the code he usually uses.

44
00:03:33,338 --> 00:03:35,882
<i>Four, one, zero.</i>

45
00:03:35,965 --> 00:03:38,509
Two, two, three.

46
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:40,220
It's open.

47
00:03:40,303 --> 00:03:41,387
Now…

48
00:03:47,435 --> 00:03:48,269
HIKARI TAKENAKA

49
00:03:48,353 --> 00:03:50,355
Nakazaki, where is the fingerprint film?

50
00:03:52,398 --> 00:03:55,652
I've seen this in anime,
but it actually works?

51
00:04:01,908 --> 00:04:03,451
Do you always do this sort of thing?

52
00:04:03,534 --> 00:04:05,536
It's a life hack.

53
00:04:08,414 --> 00:04:10,166
TRANSFERRING DATA

54
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:12,669
<i>I'm so glad Hikari</i>
<i>got to star in that commercial.</i>

55
00:04:12,752 --> 00:04:14,629
Thank you as always.

56
00:04:14,712 --> 00:04:16,839
It's all thanks to you, Mr. Tajima.

57
00:04:17,632 --> 00:04:19,425
I'm sure Nishiguchi is happy too.

58
00:04:19,509 --> 00:04:21,552
He's her manager, after all.

59
00:04:21,636 --> 00:04:24,347
He's useless,
so I was thinking of replacing him soon.

60
00:04:24,973 --> 00:04:26,432
Excuse me.

61
00:04:26,516 --> 00:04:28,351
I brought your drinks.

62
00:04:28,434 --> 00:04:29,936
Just set them down here.

63
00:04:30,019 --> 00:04:31,646
Oh, understood, sir.

64
00:04:31,729 --> 00:04:33,731
-My son's calling.
-Go ahead.

65
00:04:35,024 --> 00:04:37,485
Hey, give me a break, you bastard!

66
00:04:37,568 --> 00:04:38,820
-I'm so sorry!
-Get me a towel.

67
00:04:38,903 --> 00:04:40,571
-A towel?
-You have one right there!

68
00:04:40,655 --> 00:04:42,156
I do, sorry.

69
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:45,118
-What are you doing?
-I'm so sorry.

70
00:04:45,201 --> 00:04:46,995
-That's too many towels!
-Sorry.

71
00:04:47,078 --> 00:04:48,204
How is Yuuki doing?

72
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:50,540
Sorry. Today is canceled.
Let's reschedule.

73
00:04:50,623 --> 00:04:52,000
Why so suddenly?

74
00:04:52,083 --> 00:04:53,126
Mr. Tajima!

75
00:04:56,004 --> 00:04:57,338
I'm sorry.

76
00:04:58,631 --> 00:05:00,258
-So sorry.
-That's enough.

77
00:05:00,341 --> 00:05:02,176
Excuse me. I'm sorry!

78
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:06,889
Hello?

79
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:08,933
Sorry. I'll get changed and head over.

80
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:10,268
Okay.

81
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:17,900
I'm sorry. My apologies.

82
00:05:17,984 --> 00:05:20,320
<i>S-Sabayama here! I'm sorry.</i>

83
00:05:20,403 --> 00:05:22,322
<i>Ishikawa went back to his room!</i>

84
00:05:22,405 --> 00:05:23,948
<i>Why so soon?</i>

85
00:05:24,032 --> 00:05:26,909
<i>-How much time is left?</i>
<i>-Three minutes remaining.</i>

86
00:05:29,245 --> 00:05:30,621
I'll leave the rest to you.

87
00:05:30,705 --> 00:05:32,790
-Hey, hold on!
-Where are you going?

88
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:35,710
<i>Mr. Uramawashi, what should we do?</i>

89
00:05:35,793 --> 00:05:36,961
<i>Are you listening?</i>

90
00:05:37,045 --> 00:05:38,963
<i>We're still copying the files.</i>

91
00:05:39,464 --> 00:05:41,674
MINUTES LEFT

92
00:05:45,178 --> 00:05:46,304
Huh?

93
00:05:46,387 --> 00:05:47,972
There you are!

94
00:05:48,056 --> 00:05:51,059
I accidentally picked up your key earlier.

95
00:05:52,018 --> 00:05:52,894
I'm sorry.

96
00:05:52,977 --> 00:05:54,062
What?

97
00:05:54,145 --> 00:05:55,855
Why give him the key?

98
00:05:55,938 --> 00:05:57,482
<i>Seriously…</i>

99
00:06:03,196 --> 00:06:05,031
I am very sorry.

100
00:06:06,991 --> 00:06:08,534
You too, sir?

101
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:11,162
There is currently an issue
with the room keys.

102
00:06:11,245 --> 00:06:13,039
Please replace it at the front desk.

103
00:06:13,122 --> 00:06:14,332
Are you serious?

104
00:06:14,415 --> 00:06:16,459
We apologize for the inconvenience.

105
00:06:24,759 --> 00:06:26,469
We are very sorry.

106
00:06:27,845 --> 00:06:30,598
Of course it's a fake.

107
00:06:31,224 --> 00:06:32,391
ONE MINUTE LEFT

108
00:06:32,475 --> 00:06:33,768
DATA TRANSFER COMPLETE

109
00:06:35,645 --> 00:06:38,981
<i>-You should have told us.</i>
<i>-Sorry.</i>

110
00:06:40,316 --> 00:06:41,943
Good work, everyone.

111
00:06:47,115 --> 00:06:49,784
<i>The damages trial between</i>
<i>Mr. Shuto Ishikawa,</i>

112
00:06:49,867 --> 00:06:51,744
<i>president of an entertainment agency,</i>

113
00:06:51,828 --> 00:06:55,790
<i>and the defendant, a former manager,</i>
<i>is about to begin.</i>

114
00:06:56,582 --> 00:06:57,917
Mr. Ishikawa,

115
00:06:58,835 --> 00:07:02,922
you claim that because Hikari Takenaka,
a talent under your agency,

116
00:07:03,005 --> 00:07:05,716
dropped out of a commercial
due to Mr. Nishiguchi harassing her,

117
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:11,347
your agency had to pay
100 million yen in penalties. Correct?

118
00:07:12,098 --> 00:07:13,224
That's right.

119
00:07:13,766 --> 00:07:17,478
Because of him, our entire agency
is being slandered online.

120
00:07:17,562 --> 00:07:19,480
That's strange.

121
00:07:19,564 --> 00:07:21,858
It differs from Mr. Nishiguchi's claim.

122
00:07:22,692 --> 00:07:25,611
That means one of you is lying.

123
00:07:25,695 --> 00:07:27,822
I'm the victim here!

124
00:07:27,905 --> 00:07:30,658
-Obviously, Nishiguchi is the one lying!
-No!

125
00:07:33,327 --> 00:07:34,454
Your Honor.

126
00:07:35,037 --> 00:07:37,790
I would like to submit
additional evidence.

127
00:07:38,374 --> 00:07:40,501
COMPANY APP "RVPRO"
HAS BEEN FOUND TO BE SPYWARE

128
00:07:40,585 --> 00:07:42,837
HIKARI TAKENAKA

129
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:44,672
WHY DO YOU HAVE THOSE PHOTOS? DELETE THEM

130
00:07:44,755 --> 00:07:45,840
WE CAN LEAK THEM, THEN?

131
00:07:45,923 --> 00:07:47,675
Why do you have this data?

132
00:07:47,758 --> 00:07:51,304
You were blackmailing Hikari
and other actors,

133
00:07:51,387 --> 00:07:54,724
forcing them into work against their will.

134
00:07:54,807 --> 00:07:58,102
Your Honor, this has no relevance
to the case at hand.

135
00:07:58,186 --> 00:08:00,146
Defense counsel, please continue.

136
00:08:00,771 --> 00:08:06,068
For those who didn't comply,
you used this data to threaten them.

137
00:08:06,694 --> 00:08:08,112
WE CAN LEAK THEM, THEN?

138
00:08:08,196 --> 00:08:09,530
TO QUIT, PAY THE FIVE MILLION YEN

139
00:08:09,614 --> 00:08:11,449
PLEASE DON'T RELEASE THAT VIDEO

140
00:08:11,532 --> 00:08:13,159
No! This isn't true!

141
00:08:14,202 --> 00:08:19,332
They say that to maintain one lie,
you need twenty more.

142
00:08:24,086 --> 00:08:28,090
Scumbags who think nothing
of sacrificing others…

143
00:08:28,966 --> 00:08:30,843
shouldn't try to lie.

144
00:08:31,928 --> 00:08:32,762
Scumbags?

145
00:08:35,681 --> 00:08:40,019
Only a perfected lie
can overcome the truth.

146
00:08:43,523 --> 00:08:45,107
That is all from me.

147
00:09:04,377 --> 00:09:08,381
If you keep at this, you'll lose
your license to practice someday.

148
00:09:09,006 --> 00:09:11,759
Mr. Uramawashi, do you have a moment?

149
00:09:11,842 --> 00:09:14,345
Do you plan to pursue
the Ishikawa case further?

150
00:09:14,428 --> 00:09:17,431
There are accusations that
you obtained the evidence illegally!

151
00:09:17,515 --> 00:09:18,558
Please answer us!

152
00:09:21,811 --> 00:09:27,149
The truth was painted over with lies.
All I did was use lies to reclaim it.

153
00:09:42,790 --> 00:09:44,834
Habu! Carry this!

154
00:09:44,917 --> 00:09:46,836
But you lost at rock-paper-scissors.

155
00:09:47,837 --> 00:09:50,172
Because of that plan, my work's piling up.

156
00:09:50,256 --> 00:09:52,592
Don't spill water
on the target again, okay?

157
00:09:52,675 --> 00:09:57,638
-It succeeded, so what's the problem?
-Well, that's because I had your back.

158
00:09:58,598 --> 00:09:59,849
Bastard.

159
00:10:00,558 --> 00:10:03,185
Hey, how many times do I have to tell you!

160
00:10:03,269 --> 00:10:05,187
It's always the same thing!

161
00:10:05,271 --> 00:10:06,814
CUBE HOTEL INFILTRATION PLAN

162
00:10:06,897 --> 00:10:09,275
Nakazaki, congrats on your debut.

163
00:10:09,358 --> 00:10:11,193
You have a knack for this.

164
00:10:11,277 --> 00:10:14,280
I only wanted a normal
part-time job at a law firm.

165
00:10:14,363 --> 00:10:19,076
Boss, once again,
we are deeply in the red.

166
00:10:19,702 --> 00:10:23,497
Well, all necessary expenses,
to bring smiles to people's faces!

167
00:10:26,459 --> 00:10:28,836
Victory drinks sure taste good.

168
00:10:30,713 --> 00:10:33,799
Drinking is fine,
but please do your work properly.

169
00:10:33,883 --> 00:10:34,884
This!

170
00:10:35,509 --> 00:10:38,137
We haven't even finished
the initial blueprints!

171
00:10:40,431 --> 00:10:42,141
I'm talking to you too, Habu!

172
00:10:42,683 --> 00:10:44,352
-It's time to head home.
-What?

173
00:10:44,435 --> 00:10:45,311
-See you.
-Bye.

174
00:10:45,394 --> 00:10:47,813
Wait, we're still working, so help us out.

175
00:10:47,897 --> 00:10:49,440
We don't pay overtime.

176
00:10:50,524 --> 00:10:52,193
Wait, I don't get paid either?

177
00:10:52,276 --> 00:10:54,779
Sorry, my hours are discretionary.

178
00:10:54,862 --> 00:10:56,280
Well then, bye.

179
00:10:56,364 --> 00:10:58,240
-Wait!
-See you.

180
00:10:59,825 --> 00:11:01,577
Mr. Uramawashi!

181
00:11:01,661 --> 00:11:03,329
Is the plan revision ready yet?

182
00:11:03,412 --> 00:11:04,914
Being a lawyer is fine,

183
00:11:04,997 --> 00:11:07,375
but please focus
on the architecture side too.

184
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:11,671
This is it.

185
00:11:12,421 --> 00:11:14,799
No, this one…

186
00:11:14,882 --> 00:11:18,761
-Hey.
-Guggenheim, as designed by Gehry.

187
00:11:21,555 --> 00:11:25,351
These curves are so pretty,
no matter how many times I look at them.

188
00:11:25,434 --> 00:11:26,602
I knew it,

189
00:11:27,436 --> 00:11:31,357
we gotta go with an organic form.

190
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:32,983
No!

191
00:11:33,067 --> 00:11:34,944
Whether as a lawyer or an architect,

192
00:11:35,027 --> 00:11:38,239
shouldn't client preferences
come before your own tastes?

193
00:11:38,322 --> 00:11:40,408
Hey, work before drinking.

194
00:11:40,491 --> 00:11:45,037
Rushing won't produce
anything good, right?

195
00:11:47,164 --> 00:11:49,542
No, not until I finish work! Habu!

196
00:11:49,625 --> 00:11:51,377
-Bring that over.
-Huh?

197
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:54,839
-Can I just eat first…
-Hurry up!

198
00:11:55,756 --> 00:11:59,510
In the end, we couldn't get
Representative Tajima.

199
00:11:59,593 --> 00:12:01,720
He left so suddenly.

200
00:12:01,804 --> 00:12:04,598
He's got the devil's luck.

201
00:12:18,112 --> 00:12:19,864
By the way, he won again.

202
00:12:19,947 --> 00:12:23,159
-Won what?
-Shuto Ishikawa's trial.

203
00:12:23,242 --> 00:12:25,703
Mr. Uramawashi won brilliantly.

204
00:12:25,786 --> 00:12:28,038
I don't accept him as a lawyer.

205
00:12:28,122 --> 00:12:31,041
His hair is long,
and he doesn't dress properly in court.

206
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:33,961
Well, that part is problematic.

207
00:12:34,044 --> 00:12:38,215
But he's protecting his clients,
so as a lawyer, isn't he a good one?

208
00:12:38,799 --> 00:12:41,594
Even so, his methods are not just.

209
00:12:41,677 --> 00:12:45,514
Yukari, you are too serious.
As a lawyer, that's a weakness.

210
00:12:47,141 --> 00:12:49,435
Oh, look at the time.

211
00:12:50,269 --> 00:12:53,105
-I'm off.
-Yukari, wait!

212
00:12:53,189 --> 00:12:54,648
-Good luck.
-Yes!

213
00:12:54,732 --> 00:12:57,151
<i>President of River Productions…</i>

214
00:12:57,234 --> 00:13:00,529
He made a mess of things.

215
00:13:01,614 --> 00:13:03,616
Now is an important period for me.

216
00:13:03,699 --> 00:13:06,076
I don't want any unnecessary trouble.

217
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:08,370
All the cleanup
has already been completed.

218
00:13:08,454 --> 00:13:11,832
Oh. I'm glad you're a competent secretary.

219
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:16,962
<i>-Our next story is…</i>
-Unlike some incompetent lawyer I know!

220
00:13:17,046 --> 00:13:21,342
<i>-The murder of Ms. Chiharu Aoi, 24…</i>
-Why was he even recommended?

221
00:13:21,425 --> 00:13:26,680
<i>Padam Garty, an Ulgovian, living in Ota,</i>
<i>has been indicted for murder.</i>

222
00:13:27,473 --> 00:13:31,185
<i>So far, he has denied all accusations.</i>

223
00:13:31,268 --> 00:13:33,437
SUSPECT CLAIMS
"I DIDN'T DO IT, I KNOW NOTHING"

224
00:13:35,648 --> 00:13:37,816
Nice to meet you, Mr. Padam.

225
00:13:38,526 --> 00:13:41,362
I am attorney Yukari Aso.

226
00:13:41,445 --> 00:13:43,405
I will be your defense attorney.

227
00:13:44,031 --> 00:13:45,157
I didn't kill anyone.

228
00:13:47,159 --> 00:13:51,413
But the apartment CCTV
captured you, right?

229
00:13:52,164 --> 00:13:55,209
I only went there to deliver a package.

230
00:13:55,292 --> 00:13:57,461
No one believes me, not even the police.

231
00:13:59,088 --> 00:14:01,006
I believe you.

232
00:14:01,632 --> 00:14:05,219
So please, believe in me too.

233
00:14:06,804 --> 00:14:08,639
-Hello.
-Hello.

234
00:14:09,515 --> 00:14:10,641
Ms. Aso!

235
00:14:11,267 --> 00:14:14,228
Mr. Moriki wants you to go to his office.

236
00:14:15,646 --> 00:14:19,275
-Falsely accused?
-Yes, he denies committing the crime.

237
00:14:19,358 --> 00:14:23,279
For the prosecutors to decide to indict,
they must have a lot of evidence.

238
00:14:23,362 --> 00:14:27,241
But this case feels rushed
and based on circumstantial evidence.

239
00:14:27,324 --> 00:14:29,910
You always charge ahead
with your sense of justice,

240
00:14:29,994 --> 00:14:31,871
but can you stop that already?

241
00:14:31,954 --> 00:14:33,664
Before long, you will…

242
00:14:35,082 --> 00:14:36,208
Ouch.

243
00:14:36,917 --> 00:14:40,337
Thanks to you, Ms. Aso,
I have to keep stomach medicine on me.

244
00:14:40,421 --> 00:14:43,132
Please take care of yourself. Excuse me.

245
00:14:49,013 --> 00:14:50,180
Hello.

246
00:14:50,264 --> 00:14:51,682
Hello!

247
00:14:54,435 --> 00:14:57,563
MR. PADAM GARTY
MURDER CASE

248
00:14:59,148 --> 00:15:00,524
This case…

249
00:15:00,608 --> 00:15:02,902
You have a 0.1% chance of winning.

250
00:15:02,985 --> 00:15:05,779
We can win one in a thousand times.

251
00:15:05,863 --> 00:15:09,325
Protecting the client
is the only correct answer for a lawyer.

252
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:12,703
No chance of you giving up I see.

253
00:15:16,874 --> 00:15:19,335
JUSTICE'S FORM

254
00:15:21,837 --> 00:15:23,005
Here.

255
00:15:24,089 --> 00:15:25,925
I want a bit more openness.

256
00:15:26,008 --> 00:15:28,469
I will look into removing the partition.

257
00:15:28,552 --> 00:15:30,554
Also, I want to add more pillars.

258
00:15:30,638 --> 00:15:31,764
Pillars?

259
00:15:32,431 --> 00:15:34,600
Okay. What are the hiring conditions?

260
00:15:34,683 --> 00:15:38,979
Smart, able to read the room,
and good at lying.

261
00:15:39,063 --> 00:15:41,106
Understood. I will contact them.

262
00:15:42,316 --> 00:15:43,943
-Sabayama.
-Yes?

263
00:15:45,361 --> 00:15:48,489
Could you show me
that security camera footage?

264
00:15:48,572 --> 00:15:52,868
The police took the footage.

265
00:15:55,579 --> 00:15:57,414
But there's a backup, right?

266
00:15:57,498 --> 00:15:59,166
That was taken as well.

267
00:15:59,249 --> 00:16:01,502
"To preserve evidence," they said.

268
00:16:02,419 --> 00:16:04,004
I see.

269
00:16:05,005 --> 00:16:07,591
Then, please show me the crime scene.

270
00:16:18,185 --> 00:16:21,021
There's a breaker there?

271
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:23,774
The resident liked to keep it hidden.

272
00:16:26,151 --> 00:16:29,113
How was the body when found?

273
00:16:29,196 --> 00:16:30,781
She didn't show up for work,

274
00:16:30,864 --> 00:16:33,659
so people from the club got worried
and came to check.

275
00:16:33,742 --> 00:16:36,537
She worked as a hostess, right?

276
00:16:37,287 --> 00:16:38,288
Yes.

277
00:16:38,372 --> 00:16:42,001
She was found collapsed,
bleeding from her head.

278
00:16:42,835 --> 00:16:44,253
Right over there.

279
00:16:53,512 --> 00:16:56,640
What was Ms. Chiharu like at the club?

280
00:16:57,891 --> 00:17:02,604
Chiharu was flirty, so customers often got
the wrong idea and hit on her.

281
00:17:03,147 --> 00:17:05,774
But she actually had a boyfriend.

282
00:17:05,858 --> 00:17:07,317
She was in a relationship?

283
00:17:07,401 --> 00:17:11,238
Yes. She was always bragging
that she was dating a bigshot's son.

284
00:17:11,989 --> 00:17:13,741
And on social media,

285
00:17:14,575 --> 00:17:16,869
she was often hinting at it.

286
00:17:18,454 --> 00:17:19,455
Huh?

287
00:17:20,581 --> 00:17:22,916
I'm pretty sure there was a photo of him…

288
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,169
What kind of person was her boyfriend?

289
00:17:25,252 --> 00:17:29,214
He is the son of a Diet member,
Tajima something?

290
00:17:29,298 --> 00:17:32,342
-You shouldn't tell her that.
-He was a politician's son?

291
00:17:32,426 --> 00:17:37,806
Yes. At first she kept it a secret,
but she wanted to brag so badly.

292
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:39,600
It was totally obvious.

293
00:17:39,683 --> 00:17:42,269
-Saki, you have a customer.
-Oh, okay!

294
00:17:42,352 --> 00:17:44,271
Sorry, I was asked for.

295
00:17:44,354 --> 00:17:46,190
Wait a moment.

296
00:17:48,442 --> 00:17:51,737
-Um…
-I wasn't close with Chiharu at all.

297
00:17:52,571 --> 00:17:55,491
-This is Saki!
-Hi, Saki!

298
00:17:55,574 --> 00:17:56,617
Thank you!

299
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:58,619
Have a seat here.

300
00:18:04,708 --> 00:18:07,753
-I'LL VISIT AGAIN WHEN THINGS CALM DOWN
-REALLY? IT'S A PROMISE!

301
00:18:07,836 --> 00:18:11,048
A LAWYER CAME TO THE CLUB
SHE WAS ASKING ABOUT CHIHARU

302
00:18:13,842 --> 00:18:15,302
Shiori, you ask him too.

303
00:18:15,385 --> 00:18:19,264
-No.
-I need to give it some thought.

304
00:18:20,182 --> 00:18:23,060
The victim was apparently
in a relationship with Yuuki Tajima,

305
00:18:23,143 --> 00:18:25,771
Representative Tajima's son.
They planned for marriage.

306
00:18:25,854 --> 00:18:29,691
-You suspect him based on that?
-I am only discussing the possibility.

307
00:18:29,775 --> 00:18:34,029
-Don't look too much into this case.
-Why?!

308
00:18:34,113 --> 00:18:36,740
Consider who the players are.

309
00:18:36,824 --> 00:18:41,036
If you act recklessly,
it's not just you on the line.

310
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:44,414
So you're saying we should just discard
people who are vulnerable?

311
00:18:44,498 --> 00:18:47,793
You want me to overlook
powerful people preying on the weak?

312
00:18:47,876 --> 00:18:51,171
What is questioned in court
is not righteousness,

313
00:18:51,255 --> 00:18:53,715
but facts built up from evidence.

314
00:18:54,258 --> 00:18:58,011
If you misunderstand that,
you cannot save your client.

315
00:19:03,851 --> 00:19:09,439
On the night of the incident, Yuuki Tajima
was having dinner with his father,

316
00:19:09,523 --> 00:19:11,316
Representative Tajima.

317
00:19:13,569 --> 00:19:15,821
HAVING DINNER WITH DAD TO CATCH UP
FAMILY TIME IS NICE ONCE IN A WHILE (LOL)

318
00:19:26,957 --> 00:19:28,834
Dad, I'm sorry.

319
00:19:28,917 --> 00:19:31,545
I had no idea a paparazzi was after me.

320
00:19:33,422 --> 00:19:35,632
Please sue this weekly magazine.

321
00:19:35,716 --> 00:19:39,094
Someone told me a weirdo came
to that club, asking questions.

322
00:19:39,178 --> 00:19:40,762
Very well.

323
00:19:40,846 --> 00:19:42,931
I'll prepare the lawsuit.

324
00:19:43,015 --> 00:19:44,808
You two, don't do anything!

325
00:19:45,934 --> 00:19:47,936
I'll ask this guy to handle it.

326
00:19:50,230 --> 00:19:51,773
Uramawashi?

327
00:19:52,649 --> 00:19:54,651
But at the recent trial, he was the one--

328
00:19:54,735 --> 00:19:57,738
I'm willing to make allies out of enemies.
That's my creed.

329
00:19:58,363 --> 00:20:02,743
Compared to those losers,
he is much more promising.

330
00:20:04,536 --> 00:20:09,458
If we throw enough money at him,
Uramawashi will work for us.

331
00:20:10,042 --> 00:20:11,460
A 30 percent markup, then.

332
00:20:11,543 --> 00:20:13,337
30 percent, huh?

333
00:20:13,420 --> 00:20:15,464
If we include all your requests,

334
00:20:15,547 --> 00:20:18,217
it seems it will
slightly exceed your budget.

335
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:20,552
It might be a bit over budget.

336
00:20:20,636 --> 00:20:22,846
We can adjust based
on what you prioritize,

337
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:24,806
so let's discuss it together.

338
00:20:24,890 --> 00:20:27,893
My fee is triple the market rate.
Is that acceptable?

339
00:20:28,894 --> 00:20:30,854
Huh? Triple?

340
00:20:30,938 --> 00:20:32,189
His fees are extortion.

341
00:20:32,272 --> 00:20:34,024
I recommend you stay away from him.

342
00:20:34,608 --> 00:20:37,527
I will hear the details when I visit.

343
00:20:37,611 --> 00:20:39,571
<i>Thank you very much.</i>

344
00:20:39,655 --> 00:20:42,824
I didn't expect you to accept our offer.

345
00:20:42,908 --> 00:20:45,244
I will not disappoint.

346
00:20:57,256 --> 00:21:00,217
Next, Exhibit No.7.

347
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:03,428
This is security camera footage
from the victim's apartment.

348
00:21:03,512 --> 00:21:08,725
The defendant is seen entering and leaving
shortly before the victim's time of death,

349
00:21:08,809 --> 00:21:12,562
and with this evidence,
we plan to prove the defendant's guilt.

350
00:21:13,313 --> 00:21:16,566
After that, no one else was seen
entering or leaving the area.

351
00:21:42,718 --> 00:21:44,094
Thank you very much.

352
00:21:52,853 --> 00:21:54,438
Excuse me.

353
00:21:56,315 --> 00:21:57,357
Excuse me!

354
00:21:57,441 --> 00:21:59,609
I was saving this seat.

355
00:21:59,693 --> 00:22:01,320
What are you talking about?

356
00:22:01,403 --> 00:22:03,530
My bag… Right, my bag!

357
00:22:03,613 --> 00:22:04,948
I left my bag here.

358
00:22:05,032 --> 00:22:07,326
Do you have any proof?

359
00:22:07,409 --> 00:22:09,119
Proof?

360
00:22:09,202 --> 00:22:12,164
If you don't, stop making stuff up.

361
00:22:14,207 --> 00:22:15,625
I'm very sorry.

362
00:22:15,709 --> 00:22:17,336
There is proof.

363
00:22:28,180 --> 00:22:30,724
Huh? Mr. Uramawashi?

364
00:22:31,641 --> 00:22:33,310
How do you know of me?

365
00:22:33,393 --> 00:22:35,270
I am a lawyer too.

366
00:22:35,353 --> 00:22:36,396
So?

367
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:39,691
I'm asking where her proof is.

368
00:22:43,153 --> 00:22:46,740
That woman over there
took a selfie earlier.

369
00:22:46,823 --> 00:22:49,201
Angle-wise, it caught this seat.

370
00:22:49,951 --> 00:22:52,370
Also, a delivery truck passed by.

371
00:22:52,454 --> 00:22:54,414
The dashcam should've caught this too.

372
00:22:54,498 --> 00:22:55,874
What?

373
00:22:55,957 --> 00:22:59,753
I've written down the plate number.
Shall we try contacting them?

374
00:23:02,380 --> 00:23:05,092
Very well. I just need to move, right?

375
00:23:06,259 --> 00:23:10,055
Only in Japan can you reserve a seat
just by leaving your bag!

376
00:23:12,766 --> 00:23:14,309
It's our victory.

377
00:23:14,976 --> 00:23:17,813
-Go ahead.
-You lied about the selfie.

378
00:23:17,896 --> 00:23:20,690
That lady doesn't seem
like she takes selfies.

379
00:23:20,774 --> 00:23:24,653
Besides,
I'm sure no delivery truck passed by.

380
00:23:25,987 --> 00:23:28,532
Your observation skills aren't half-bad.

381
00:23:28,615 --> 00:23:31,868
I don't want to sit in a seat
obtained through a lie.

382
00:23:31,952 --> 00:23:33,328
You didn't obtain it.

383
00:23:34,246 --> 00:23:36,998
You reclaimed what was yours,
through a lie.

384
00:23:43,672 --> 00:23:45,715
If there were no lies in this world,

385
00:23:45,799 --> 00:23:50,220
we would never have to doubt each other,
or worry about hidden intentions.

386
00:23:50,929 --> 00:23:52,430
Because some people lie,

387
00:23:52,514 --> 00:23:55,392
even people who do not lie
end up being suspects.

388
00:23:55,475 --> 00:23:57,602
Your ideals are beautiful.

389
00:23:57,686 --> 00:23:58,937
Is that a bad thing?

390
00:24:00,438 --> 00:24:04,025
You are like Le Corbusier's Villa Savoye.

391
00:24:08,280 --> 00:24:11,950
<i>Something urgent came up,</i>
<i>so please let me reschedule.</i>

392
00:24:12,033 --> 00:24:14,786
I don't really understand. Excuse me.

393
00:24:23,545 --> 00:24:26,089
I scanned all of her investigation files.

394
00:24:26,173 --> 00:24:27,841
How was it?

395
00:24:28,425 --> 00:24:31,636
She is not my enemy.

396
00:24:36,391 --> 00:24:39,019
Oh, you seem tired.

397
00:24:39,102 --> 00:24:40,896
A lot happened.

398
00:24:40,979 --> 00:24:43,064
Oh, hey!

399
00:24:43,148 --> 00:24:46,526
They say Yuuki Tajima is suing
this weekly magazine!

400
00:24:47,652 --> 00:24:49,529
-Due to the Chiharu article.
-Yeah.

401
00:24:49,613 --> 00:24:52,490
Attorney Uramawashi took the case.

402
00:24:52,574 --> 00:24:53,408
Huh?

403
00:24:53,491 --> 00:24:55,911
It's not related to Mr. Padam's trial,

404
00:24:55,994 --> 00:24:58,747
but you never know
what they might do, so be careful.

405
00:24:59,998 --> 00:25:04,336
Why did he agree
to defend Tajima's son anyway?

406
00:25:05,253 --> 00:25:08,924
Wouldn't it be better to defeat the son
to help that Padam guy?

407
00:25:09,758 --> 00:25:11,468
You're a real idiot, aren't you?

408
00:25:11,551 --> 00:25:12,761
An idiot?

409
00:25:12,844 --> 00:25:13,845
An idiot!

410
00:25:13,929 --> 00:25:17,599
Even if he defeats the son, he'll miss
the main target, Representative Tajima.

411
00:25:17,682 --> 00:25:20,477
He must help them in court
to gain their trust. Right?

412
00:25:20,560 --> 00:25:23,688
Very good, Nakazaki.
You aren't like Sabayama.

413
00:25:23,772 --> 00:25:26,650
-Thank you very much.
-Hey, I knew that too, you know.

414
00:25:26,733 --> 00:25:29,069
-I was just--
-Excuse me!

415
00:25:29,152 --> 00:25:31,863
-I came for an interview!
-Welcome, we've been waiting.

416
00:25:31,947 --> 00:25:33,490
-Who is that?
-Nice to meet you.

417
00:25:33,573 --> 00:25:34,991
She's interviewing for our next job.

418
00:25:35,075 --> 00:25:36,993
-Hello.
-Hello.

419
00:25:37,077 --> 00:25:37,994
TODAY'S TRENDING ARTICLE

420
00:25:38,078 --> 00:25:43,124
Because of this article, people are
leaving comments, claiming I'm the killer.

421
00:25:43,208 --> 00:25:48,797
The quickest way is to get that foreigner
named Padam to confess.

422
00:25:49,464 --> 00:25:51,174
Can you do that?

423
00:25:51,258 --> 00:25:53,176
He is ignorant of the law.

424
00:25:54,552 --> 00:25:58,390
If we tell him we'll protect his family
from forced deportation,

425
00:25:59,015 --> 00:26:00,308
he'll work with us.

426
00:26:02,143 --> 00:26:06,815
That way, Yuuki's name won't be tarnished.

427
00:26:12,696 --> 00:26:13,905
Excuse me.

428
00:26:19,160 --> 00:26:20,370
By the way,

429
00:26:21,579 --> 00:26:24,332
what were you doing
on the night of the murder?

430
00:26:26,668 --> 00:26:27,627
What?

431
00:26:28,962 --> 00:26:31,464
-Are you suspecting me?
-No.

432
00:26:32,632 --> 00:26:36,720
In order to protect you,
I want to know the truth.

433
00:26:37,846 --> 00:26:41,891
Hypothetically, even if they suspect you
are involved in the murder,

434
00:26:41,975 --> 00:26:47,188
if you tell the truth,
we can get a suspended sentence.

435
00:26:47,772 --> 00:26:48,982
Maybe.

436
00:26:51,568 --> 00:26:54,779
Depending on the intent,
the verdict varies greatly.

437
00:26:57,490 --> 00:26:59,284
I see.

438
00:27:01,036 --> 00:27:04,998
Around 7:00 p.m., the time of the crime,
where were you?

439
00:27:06,499 --> 00:27:09,169
On that day, after work,
I went out for dinner.

440
00:27:09,252 --> 00:27:10,378
Dinner?

441
00:27:11,087 --> 00:27:12,047
With whom?

442
00:27:12,672 --> 00:27:16,009
Yuuki was having dinner
with Representative Tajima.

443
00:27:16,092 --> 00:27:17,635
We have proof.

444
00:27:20,388 --> 00:27:22,807
Chiharu was just a girl
I fooled around with.

445
00:27:22,891 --> 00:27:24,726
I had no reason to kill her.

446
00:27:25,477 --> 00:27:27,312
Ever been to her apartment?

447
00:27:27,395 --> 00:27:28,646
No.

448
00:27:30,315 --> 00:27:31,191
Not even once?

449
00:27:33,693 --> 00:27:34,527
Nope.

450
00:27:35,737 --> 00:27:36,946
Very well.

451
00:27:49,459 --> 00:27:51,836
LEMON GASUI

452
00:29:15,879 --> 00:29:17,422
It's done.

453
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:22,927
A blueprint of lies.

454
00:29:24,637 --> 00:29:27,056
Ms. Konno, room B, please.

455
00:29:27,140 --> 00:29:28,683
The most expensive spot.

456
00:29:28,767 --> 00:29:32,562
-Habu, take the dimensions from the model.
-Got it. I'll draft the layouts.

457
00:29:32,645 --> 00:29:34,814
Is this 1 to 30?
Match it with the wall surface.

458
00:29:34,898 --> 00:29:37,484
-I know.
-Nakazaki, samples for the cross-panels.

459
00:29:37,567 --> 00:29:38,443
Okay.

460
00:29:38,526 --> 00:29:41,988
Sabayama, verify the materials
and list interior finishes and equipment.

461
00:29:42,071 --> 00:29:44,949
-Okay.
-Oh, right. Ms. Konno.

462
00:29:45,784 --> 00:29:47,410
Handle this too.

463
00:29:48,328 --> 00:29:49,704
What is this for?

464
00:29:49,788 --> 00:29:52,624
-Won't concrete work for the aging finish?
-I know.

465
00:29:52,707 --> 00:29:55,960
-Search online for the circled parts here.
-Excuse me.

466
00:29:56,044 --> 00:29:59,631
I am Yukari Aso,
an attorney from Cordia Law Firm.

467
00:30:03,551 --> 00:30:04,552
Huh?

468
00:30:04,636 --> 00:30:07,347
Wait, is this Mr. Uramawashi's office?

469
00:30:07,430 --> 00:30:09,432
Mr. Uramawashi is in that room.

470
00:30:10,308 --> 00:30:13,019
I'm sorry. Excuse me.

471
00:30:13,102 --> 00:30:14,437
Sorry.

472
00:30:18,775 --> 00:30:20,485
Have we met somewhere before?

473
00:30:20,568 --> 00:30:22,695
-No. This is our first meeting.
-No…

474
00:30:22,779 --> 00:30:25,323
-I've met you--
-Why have you come to see him?

475
00:30:25,406 --> 00:30:27,450
-I will guide you.
-No need.

476
00:30:31,287 --> 00:30:32,914
Mr. Uramawashi. Excuse me!

477
00:30:32,997 --> 00:30:36,251
I am Yukari Aso,
an attorney from Cordia Law Firm.

478
00:30:36,960 --> 00:30:38,419
I met you the other day.

479
00:30:38,503 --> 00:30:40,505
Mr. Padam suddenly confessed.

480
00:30:40,588 --> 00:30:42,423
What on earth did you say to him?

481
00:30:43,007 --> 00:30:46,761
The person who killed Chiharu Aoi
might be Yuuki Tajima.

482
00:30:46,845 --> 00:30:49,889
They used influence
to pin the crime on Mr. Padam.

483
00:30:51,516 --> 00:30:53,852
Hey, what are you doing?

484
00:30:53,935 --> 00:30:55,645
I'm in the middle of an interview.

485
00:31:05,405 --> 00:31:07,490
This lawyer is calling me a killer.

486
00:31:07,574 --> 00:31:09,617
I'm going to sue her for defamation!

487
00:31:09,701 --> 00:31:10,535
What?

488
00:31:10,618 --> 00:31:12,912
Why her and not the publisher?

489
00:31:12,996 --> 00:31:14,998
It will show them we mean business.

490
00:31:15,081 --> 00:31:16,249
Wait a minute.

491
00:31:16,332 --> 00:31:20,253
What if this creates more trouble?
Making an enemy out of a lawyer--

492
00:31:20,336 --> 00:31:21,713
Don't interfere!

493
00:31:26,050 --> 00:31:27,552
Mr. Uramawashi.

494
00:31:28,344 --> 00:31:30,722
I leave this up to you.

495
00:31:33,433 --> 00:31:35,143
TOKYO DISTRICT COURT

496
00:31:39,480 --> 00:31:43,359
INDICTMENT
DEFENDANT - YUKARI ASO

497
00:31:45,987 --> 00:31:48,781
Ms. Aso, don't worry.
Even if you lose the trial, it's okay.

498
00:31:48,865 --> 00:31:51,743
It's not like your life is over.
Just do your best.

499
00:31:53,119 --> 00:31:57,457
No, I can't help.
I'm insanely busy right now.

500
00:31:57,540 --> 00:31:59,042
It's fine.

501
00:31:59,125 --> 00:32:00,919
I will defend myself.

502
00:32:01,461 --> 00:32:05,715
What wins in court is not influence,
but justice, right?

503
00:32:07,258 --> 00:32:08,927
Thanks for waiting!

504
00:32:09,010 --> 00:32:10,178
I'm here.

505
00:32:10,261 --> 00:32:12,388
Sorry, my mistake!

506
00:32:12,472 --> 00:32:13,848
There you are!

507
00:32:16,184 --> 00:32:20,146
I got plenty of cute girls
for you, Mr. Uramawashi.

508
00:32:20,229 --> 00:32:21,522
Why thank you.

509
00:32:21,606 --> 00:32:24,233
I'll stick with you all night.

510
00:32:25,193 --> 00:32:29,864
Alright, then,
as a rally before the decisive battle,

511
00:32:29,948 --> 00:32:32,116
everyone's drinking tonight!

512
00:32:32,200 --> 00:32:34,661
Yay! Cheers!

513
00:32:34,744 --> 00:32:36,162
-First time here?
-Yes.

514
00:32:36,245 --> 00:32:37,705
I'm Ai. Nice to meet you.

515
00:32:37,789 --> 00:32:40,208
-Nice, Ai! Let's toast!
-Hang on!

516
00:32:40,291 --> 00:32:41,709
-Here, Ai.
-May I?

517
00:32:41,793 --> 00:32:44,212
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

518
00:32:51,761 --> 00:32:53,221
Hey, Yuuki.

519
00:32:53,304 --> 00:32:54,555
Let's go home together.

520
00:32:54,639 --> 00:32:55,974
Should we?

521
00:32:56,057 --> 00:32:57,558
Sorry, I'll head out first!

522
00:32:58,643 --> 00:33:00,770
Mr. Uramawashi, I'm heading out.

523
00:33:00,853 --> 00:33:03,481
-Allow me to drive you two home.
-Really?

524
00:33:03,564 --> 00:33:04,649
I haven't drunk.

525
00:33:04,732 --> 00:33:06,693
-How nice!
-You mean it?

526
00:33:06,776 --> 00:33:08,861
-Well then, please do.
-Huh?

527
00:33:27,672 --> 00:33:29,132
Ai?

528
00:33:43,146 --> 00:33:44,355
Huh?

529
00:33:49,652 --> 00:33:50,903
What?

530
00:33:52,321 --> 00:33:53,531
This room…

531
00:33:54,991 --> 00:33:55,825
What?

532
00:33:58,536 --> 00:34:00,371
Will you be all right tomorrow?

533
00:34:01,205 --> 00:34:04,083
At the last hearing,
I pointed out traces of editing

534
00:34:04,167 --> 00:34:06,753
in the apartment's CCTV footage,

535
00:34:07,670 --> 00:34:10,757
and they haven't been able to explain it.

536
00:34:11,591 --> 00:34:15,219
I believe they edited the footage
to remove Yuuki Tajima from it.

537
00:34:15,303 --> 00:34:17,680
Then, you will go all out.

538
00:34:18,306 --> 00:34:19,307
Yes!

539
00:34:21,934 --> 00:34:25,229
<i>We will now begin the witness examination.</i>

540
00:34:25,813 --> 00:34:30,276
Regarding the CCTV footage
claim made by the defendant last time,

541
00:34:30,359 --> 00:34:33,821
we have Mr. Igawa,
the apartment manager, joining us.

542
00:34:34,530 --> 00:34:39,077
You were habitually committing mail theft.

543
00:34:39,994 --> 00:34:45,666
In order to erase that evidence,
you edited the security camera footage.

544
00:34:45,750 --> 00:34:47,126
What?

545
00:34:47,877 --> 00:34:49,629
I am very sorry.

546
00:34:49,712 --> 00:34:54,675
There is no footage remaining
from the day of the incident.

547
00:34:56,177 --> 00:34:57,011
Correct.

548
00:34:57,095 --> 00:34:58,096
Objection!

549
00:34:58,846 --> 00:35:00,765
Are you covering for someone?

550
00:35:00,848 --> 00:35:02,266
Please speak truthfully.

551
00:35:02,350 --> 00:35:03,518
I'm not lying!

552
00:35:04,143 --> 00:35:05,436
It's the truth.

553
00:35:20,159 --> 00:35:21,702
PLAINTIFF EXAMINATION

554
00:35:23,746 --> 00:35:27,583
We will now begin
the examination of the plaintiff himself.

555
00:35:27,667 --> 00:35:30,128
Plaintiff's counsel, please proceed.

556
00:35:33,673 --> 00:35:34,882
Mr. Tajima,

557
00:35:36,300 --> 00:35:43,266
the defendant stated to a reporter
that you murdered Chiharu Aoi.

558
00:35:43,349 --> 00:35:45,309
Is this true or false?

559
00:35:45,893 --> 00:35:47,228
False.

560
00:35:47,311 --> 00:35:49,564
You have never been to her place either.

561
00:35:49,647 --> 00:35:50,940
Of course not.

562
00:35:51,816 --> 00:35:57,488
Your Honor,
may I ask questions using Exhibit No.5?

563
00:35:57,572 --> 00:35:58,823
Granted.

564
00:36:02,243 --> 00:36:03,452
Huh? This…

565
00:36:03,536 --> 00:36:07,623
This room is an exact recreation
of the room where Ms. Aoi lived,

566
00:36:07,707 --> 00:36:09,917
before she was murdered.

567
00:36:10,001 --> 00:36:12,420
What is the meaning of this?

568
00:36:12,503 --> 00:36:15,214
I took the liberty of testing you
based on my judgment.

569
00:36:15,298 --> 00:36:16,215
Testing?

570
00:36:16,299 --> 00:36:18,509
It is to protect you.

571
00:36:19,719 --> 00:36:24,390
Hypothetically, if Mr. Tajima
had murdered Ms. Aoi,

572
00:36:25,308 --> 00:36:29,854
waking up and realizing he is at her place
should make him agitated, but!

573
00:36:29,937 --> 00:36:31,105
Take a look.

574
00:36:31,772 --> 00:36:34,525
He is completely calm.

575
00:36:34,609 --> 00:36:36,444
He is clearly agitated.

576
00:36:38,446 --> 00:36:39,655
<i>Huh?</i>

577
00:36:41,199 --> 00:36:44,577
Then, inconveniently, a blackout happened.

578
00:36:45,494 --> 00:36:47,830
He is obviously agitated, isn't he?

579
00:36:47,914 --> 00:36:51,918
-Why does he know where the breaker is?
-Please don't speak out of line.

580
00:36:52,001 --> 00:36:56,172
You just happened
to see the breaker, right?

581
00:36:56,255 --> 00:36:57,548
That's right.

582
00:37:04,430 --> 00:37:08,309
Even when running out of the room,
the plaintiff avoided a specific spot!

583
00:37:08,392 --> 00:37:11,437
That is the spot where
Ms. Aoi was found dead.

584
00:37:11,520 --> 00:37:13,272
You have been there before!

585
00:37:13,356 --> 00:37:15,650
Please do not speak out of line.

586
00:37:15,733 --> 00:37:20,738
Ms. Aso's statements are all forced logic.

587
00:37:20,821 --> 00:37:24,533
But… You can't dismiss this
as mere coincidence.

588
00:37:25,576 --> 00:37:27,787
If you want to make that claim,

589
00:37:28,579 --> 00:37:33,209
there is one more
piece of evidence that solidifies

590
00:37:34,418 --> 00:37:35,670
Mr. Tajima's innocence.

591
00:37:37,964 --> 00:37:40,258
Mr. Igawa, the apartment manager,

592
00:37:40,341 --> 00:37:43,427
deleted the CCTV footage
from the day of the murder,

593
00:37:43,511 --> 00:37:45,638
to hide his own theft.

594
00:37:47,265 --> 00:37:48,349
But we recovered it.

595
00:37:50,309 --> 00:37:51,352
Order in the court!

596
00:37:53,187 --> 00:37:54,981
If you check this,

597
00:37:55,064 --> 00:37:58,859
you will see that Mr. Tajima
does not appear on camera.

598
00:37:58,943 --> 00:38:00,027
Hey!

599
00:38:02,446 --> 00:38:05,241
With this, your innocence will be proven.

600
00:38:05,324 --> 00:38:06,784
Wait! Stop going off-script!

601
00:38:06,867 --> 00:38:08,119
Order in the court!

602
00:38:16,085 --> 00:38:19,714
I found it in your car the other day,
when I was driving you home.

603
00:38:21,507 --> 00:38:22,508
No…

604
00:38:22,591 --> 00:38:23,676
It's not mine!

605
00:38:24,760 --> 00:38:28,639
Isn't that the nail that was on
Ms. Aoi's index finger?

606
00:38:29,849 --> 00:38:32,518
The corpse's index finger
was missing its nail.

607
00:38:32,601 --> 00:38:34,812
It came off while you were fighting?

608
00:38:34,895 --> 00:38:35,896
Impossible!

609
00:38:36,480 --> 00:38:37,690
There's just no way!

610
00:38:37,773 --> 00:38:40,776
So the one who killed
Aoi Chiharu really was you!

611
00:38:40,860 --> 00:38:42,903
That is merely your speculation.

612
00:38:45,448 --> 00:38:47,908
Yuuki, calm down.

613
00:38:48,534 --> 00:38:51,704
If I show this footage,
the truth will be revealed.

614
00:38:53,456 --> 00:38:57,126
Your Honor, please play the video.

615
00:38:58,753 --> 00:39:01,255
-She fell on her own!
-Yuuki!

616
00:39:01,339 --> 00:39:03,799
-I didn't kill her!
-Yuuki!

617
00:39:11,182 --> 00:39:13,184
Please wait a moment.

618
00:39:14,226 --> 00:39:15,728
Does that mean

619
00:39:17,271 --> 00:39:19,732
you were lying?

620
00:39:20,441 --> 00:39:21,484
Am I correct?

621
00:39:21,567 --> 00:39:23,402
It was an accident!

622
00:39:23,486 --> 00:39:26,864
I just pushed her, and she fell,
I had no intent to kill her!

623
00:39:26,947 --> 00:39:29,867
If I tell the truth,
I'll get a suspended sentence, right?

624
00:39:35,623 --> 00:39:37,124
Your lies…

625
00:39:37,875 --> 00:39:39,251
have no beauty to them.

626
00:39:44,673 --> 00:39:46,300
Attorney Aso.

627
00:39:48,302 --> 00:39:50,554
Things have taken an unexpected turn.

628
00:39:50,638 --> 00:39:54,392
While I do regret it, I wish you the best.

629
00:39:55,559 --> 00:39:56,394
Your Honor.

630
00:39:57,353 --> 00:40:00,147
I have no further questions.

631
00:40:18,916 --> 00:40:21,043
Ai, you did great.

632
00:40:21,127 --> 00:40:22,169
Two envelopes?

633
00:40:22,253 --> 00:40:24,505
We'll call you when we need you again.

634
00:40:24,588 --> 00:40:26,424
Wait, you're paying me this much?

635
00:40:26,507 --> 00:40:30,386
In the end, he was lying about restoring
the CCTV footage, right?

636
00:40:30,469 --> 00:40:31,429
-Yeah.
-Yeah!

637
00:40:31,512 --> 00:40:33,139
That disc was empty.

638
00:40:33,722 --> 00:40:36,976
The nail was also fake. We copied it
from Chiharu's social media.

639
00:40:37,059 --> 00:40:41,272
By pretending to save the son,
he got close to Representative Tajima.

640
00:40:41,856 --> 00:40:44,733
In doing so,
he ended up taking down both of them.

641
00:40:44,817 --> 00:40:46,944
-A job well done.
-Nakazaki.

642
00:40:47,027 --> 00:40:49,655
-Yes!
-Can I take all this with me?

643
00:40:49,738 --> 00:40:51,740
-Sure.
-Here we go.

644
00:40:51,824 --> 00:40:56,704
By the way, that alibi photo,
he knew it was fake from the start.

645
00:40:56,787 --> 00:40:59,081
-Really?
-Hey, out of the way!

646
00:40:59,165 --> 00:41:00,583
The road in the background…

647
00:41:00,666 --> 00:41:02,918
At 7:00 p.m. that day,
there was no traffic jam.

648
00:41:03,002 --> 00:41:06,297
So he knew and played along!

649
00:41:06,380 --> 00:41:08,215
I'm glad he's our ally.

650
00:41:08,299 --> 00:41:10,176
As an enemy, he's terrifying!

651
00:41:15,973 --> 00:41:19,685
<i>Naoto Uramawashi, you committed acts</i>
<i>against the interests of your client,</i>

652
00:41:19,768 --> 00:41:23,772
and violated your duty of good faith.

653
00:41:25,024 --> 00:41:28,235
Pursuant to Article 56,
Paragraph One of the Attorneys Act,

654
00:41:28,319 --> 00:41:31,113
you are hereby suspended from practice.

655
00:41:31,197 --> 00:41:34,325
You are not fit to be a lawyer.

656
00:41:35,201 --> 00:41:36,785
Do you have any last words?

657
00:41:45,961 --> 00:41:48,255
Eileen Gray once said…

658
00:41:48,339 --> 00:41:50,591
"To create,

659
00:41:51,383 --> 00:41:54,178
one must first question everything."

660
00:41:55,596 --> 00:41:56,805
That's all.

661
00:42:02,228 --> 00:42:03,687
Eileen?

662
00:42:04,480 --> 00:42:05,689
Who's that?

663
00:42:06,190 --> 00:42:07,566
Do you know?

664
00:42:09,860 --> 00:42:12,696
The Japanese branch is now on track.

665
00:42:12,780 --> 00:42:14,907
Yes, impressive.

666
00:42:16,992 --> 00:42:18,285
Like father, like son.

667
00:42:18,369 --> 00:42:19,954
Thank you very much.

668
00:42:21,622 --> 00:42:23,499
You have a guest.

669
00:42:25,626 --> 00:42:27,002
Sorry to disturb your meal.

670
00:42:27,628 --> 00:42:28,837
Mr. Furuse!

671
00:42:28,921 --> 00:42:30,005
I am…

672
00:42:30,089 --> 00:42:32,341
I am sorry for being late.

673
00:42:32,424 --> 00:42:33,717
Sorry for--

674
00:42:33,801 --> 00:42:37,346
My office received some photos,
sent anonymously.

675
00:42:37,429 --> 00:42:39,974
-Oh.
-Along with proof of your illegal conduct.

676
00:42:40,057 --> 00:42:40,891
What?

677
00:42:45,437 --> 00:42:48,482
Was it Mr. Ishikawa?
So you were meeting with him?

678
00:42:49,567 --> 00:42:51,944
-This…
-Are you hiding something from me?

679
00:42:53,904 --> 00:42:54,947
I am very sorry!

680
00:42:55,656 --> 00:42:58,867
-But--
-Please, stand up.

681
00:43:00,661 --> 00:43:02,871
Your son's problem is more important.

682
00:43:03,622 --> 00:43:05,916
It is no longer just your personal issue,

683
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:08,669
it could spell trouble
for our entire party.

684
00:43:08,752 --> 00:43:10,212
You understand, right?

685
00:43:11,922 --> 00:43:13,549
My apologies, but…

686
00:43:15,467 --> 00:43:16,844
Murata.

687
00:43:16,927 --> 00:43:19,513
I'll need you to come back here soon.

688
00:43:19,597 --> 00:43:20,723
I understand.

689
00:43:20,806 --> 00:43:22,808
-Sorry.
-Wait!

690
00:43:22,891 --> 00:43:25,352
-It's no problem.
-Mr. Tajima.

691
00:43:25,436 --> 00:43:29,106
Sir! Wait…

692
00:43:29,189 --> 00:43:30,691
This is good!

693
00:43:30,774 --> 00:43:32,109
Right?

694
00:43:32,192 --> 00:43:35,070
I'm glad Mr. Padam got an acquittal.

695
00:43:35,154 --> 00:43:36,614
Thank you very much.

696
00:43:36,697 --> 00:43:40,075
I don't want to admit it,
but it's thanks to Mr. Uramawashi.

697
00:43:40,159 --> 00:43:41,118
Is that so?

698
00:43:41,702 --> 00:43:45,748
Good timing, then.
I'd like to ask you to monitor him.

699
00:43:45,831 --> 00:43:46,874
Huh?

700
00:43:47,583 --> 00:43:50,669
If he keeps on being reckless,

701
00:43:50,753 --> 00:43:54,006
it will affect the credibility
of our bar association.

702
00:43:54,089 --> 00:43:58,552
-I'm asking you, as the President--
-Wait, I can't do it!

703
00:43:58,636 --> 00:44:00,179
I really can't.

704
00:44:00,262 --> 00:44:05,100
Because you were sued, our office
was busy handling complaints, you know.

705
00:44:06,518 --> 00:44:08,854
It was really tough!

706
00:44:09,897 --> 00:44:11,357
I'll do it.

707
00:44:12,941 --> 00:44:13,776
Thank you.

708
00:44:14,985 --> 00:44:18,739
I'm not asking you to see him daily.
Just check on him a few days a week.

709
00:44:19,657 --> 00:44:20,741
Okay.

710
00:44:21,867 --> 00:44:24,828
Besides, he said you passed, too.

711
00:44:24,912 --> 00:44:27,289
-What are you talking about?
-Do your best.

712
00:44:29,124 --> 00:44:32,169
So, I will be visiting you starting today.

713
00:44:36,173 --> 00:44:39,009
Don't fool around.
We have to start closing your office.

714
00:44:39,093 --> 00:44:41,970
Delete your home page,
hide any signs you have outside.

715
00:44:42,054 --> 00:44:43,764
I don't have either.

716
00:44:43,847 --> 00:44:45,766
Please don't lie to me.

717
00:44:46,433 --> 00:44:50,896
I was so busy suing you, Aso,
my architectural work has been piling up.

718
00:44:50,979 --> 00:44:51,855
What?

719
00:44:51,939 --> 00:44:54,066
Mr. Uramawashi, you are an architect?

720
00:45:03,909 --> 00:45:07,413
More importantly,
when did you start lying?

721
00:45:08,580 --> 00:45:10,582
Did you leak info to the weekly magazine

722
00:45:10,666 --> 00:45:13,127
so that Yuuki Tajima
would request your defense?

723
00:45:13,210 --> 00:45:17,131
Did you sue me in a civil trial
just to drag him to court?

724
00:45:17,756 --> 00:45:19,466
Not bad.

725
00:45:20,426 --> 00:45:22,052
But it's all so boring.

726
00:45:25,389 --> 00:45:27,307
Please, at least answer me this.

727
00:45:27,391 --> 00:45:29,685
Why did you get suspended
from being a lawyer?

728
00:45:30,477 --> 00:45:32,396
For someone as sharp as you,

729
00:45:32,479 --> 00:45:36,692
there must have been ways to corner
the Tajimas without being suspended!

730
00:45:39,528 --> 00:45:41,447
I got tired of being a lawyer.

731
00:45:41,530 --> 00:45:42,781
-What?
-That's a lie.

732
00:45:43,490 --> 00:45:44,700
What?!

733
00:45:45,951 --> 00:45:48,787
Right now, you are an architect,
not a lawyer!

734
00:45:49,455 --> 00:45:52,541
<i>The evidence of his violence</i>
<i>still remains in the video!</i>

735
00:45:52,624 --> 00:45:55,878
<i>-He hasn't found out yet?</i>
<i>-I will fight fair and square and win.</i>

736
00:45:55,961 --> 00:45:59,381
<i>If they become the main developers,</i>
<i>they can make a lot more money…</i>

737
00:45:59,465 --> 00:46:00,507
<i>His lies.</i>

738
00:46:00,591 --> 00:46:01,633
I'll expose them.

739
00:46:01,717 --> 00:46:06,430
Careless words invite ruin.
I'll make sure you never defend again.

740
00:46:07,097 --> 00:46:08,056
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
